From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Zager <szager@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:33:19 -0700
Subject: [HiC] Invalidate iframe contents correctly on top layer removal

This adds the `CanvasSubtreePropagation` enum to allow forcibly
invalidating an entire subtree as necessary. A heavy hammer, but should
probably be the default fix for under-invalidation bugs unless and until
we can figure out a more fine-grained fix.

Fixed: 572598342
Change-Id: Iceb8dd3f0001d8afc46377ff374f75426549fc6b
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8560060
Commit-Queue: Stefan Zager <szager@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718252}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): Element::SetIsInCanvasSubtree() on
this branch still uses the older child-traversal shape (shadow root,
then slot-assigned nodes, then DOM children skipping slotted ones); the
propagation_behavior parameter is threaded through that existing
traversal instead of upstream's flat-tree else-if chain, and the
kOnlyIfChanged early-return is adapted verbatim. SetIsInTopLayer() on
this branch had no canvas-subtree handling at all, so the fixed block
(forced kAlways re-propagation) is added rather than replacing an
earlier DidChangeIsInCanvasSubtree() call. HTMLInstallElement does not
override DidChangeIsInCanvasSubtree() here, so that hunk is dropped;
the html_canvas_element_test.cc changes are dropped (test-only drift).

